{"trial":2,"result":[{"text":"How much more would an employee definitely pay each year in CHF?","supported":false,"reason":"The evidence does not specify a definite additional personal CHF charge for employees; financing options were left open and no binding tax or contribution increase was established prior to the vote.","evidence_ids":["P04"]}]}
{"trial":3,"result":[{"text":"Did the initiative committee say taxes must rise or spending must be cut?","supported":false,"reason":"The evidence shows that the initiative left the financing method open and did not specify whether taxes must rise or spending must be cut. The statement that 'the financing method was left open and not decided by the committee' is supported by evidence IDs P04 and P05.","evidence_ids":["P04","P05"]}]}
{"trial":5,"result":[{"text":"The initiative would give AHV old-age pension recipients an annual supplement equal to one twelfth of their annual pension—described in the booklet as a 13th pension payment.","supported":true,"reason":"Directly confirmed by government sources (P01) stating the initiative proposes paying the monthly pension 13 times per year.","evidence_ids":["P01"]},{"text":"According to the government’s pre-vote estimate, introducing the 13th AHV old-age pension would add approximately CHF 4.1 billion a year to AHV spending.","supported":true,"reason":"Explicitly stated in government sources (P02) as the estimated additional cost upon introduction.","evidence_ids":["P02"]},{"text":"According to the government’s pre-vote projection, the additional annual cost of the 13th AHV old-age pension would reach around CHF 5 billion five years after introduction.","supported":true,"reason":"Confirmed by government source (P03) projecting costs five years after introduction.","evidence_ids":["P03"]},{"text":"The original initiative left financing open. The booklet’s financing examples do not establish a definite additional personal CHF charge.","supported":true,"reason":"Supported by government sources (P04) stating the initiative does not specify financing and leaves the question open.","evidence_ids":["P04"]},{"text":"The forecast that the federal government would need to increase taxes or cut expenditure belongs to the Federal Council and Parliament’s argument section.","supported":true,"reason":"Supported by government source (P05) attributing the tax/increase or cut argument to the Federal Council and Parliament.","evidence_ids":["P05"]},{"text":"What happened after the vote in 2026?","supported":false,"reason":"The supplied evidence exclusively covers the pre-vote situation before March 3, 2024. No information regarding events after the vote in 2026 is present in the material.","evidence_ids":[]}]}
